# Googlebook OS on SM-T870: the tablet's health HAL with the Samsung battery driver's
# state-of-health (fg_asoc) and cycle-count (battery_cycle) nodes configured
# (T870-araclar/pil-sagligi, yamalar/pil_sagligi.py).
#
# It replaces the LineageOS vendor service vendor.health-samsung
# (/vendor/etc/init/android.hardware.health-service.samsung.rc). An "override" cannot do that
# from /product: init refuses to override a service "across the treble boundary" (vendor and
# odm files are parsed in the vendor_init subcontext, product files are not;
# system/core/init/service_parser.cpp EndSection). Instead the vendor service is stopped before
# its class starts ("stop" on a service that has not started yet keeps class_start from
# starting it, init/service.cpp StopOrReset) and this one serves IHealth/default in its place,
# with the same class, user, groups, capabilities and files. vendor.charger (off-mode
# charging, class charger) is not touched and keeps running the vendor binary.

on early-init
    stop vendor.health-samsung

service gbos.health-samsung /product/bin/hw/android.hardware.health-service.samsung-gbos
    class hal
    user system
    group system
    capabilities WAKE_ALARM BLOCK_SUSPEND
    file /dev/kmsg w

# vndservicemanager restarts the whole hal class when it restarts ("onrestart class_restart hal",
# without --only-enabled), which starts the stopped vendor service too. Its registration of
# IHealth/default would replace this one; stop it again and register this one anew.
on property:init.svc.vendor.health-samsung=running
    stop vendor.health-samsung
    restart gbos.health-samsung
